Author: Samuel He <samuelhe52@outlook.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 00:26:09 2026 +0800

    perf: Complete required ACKs under the state read lock
    
    An ACK-waiting write took the NodeState write lock a second time only to
    clear its receipt's required-ACK list and release the retained bytes.
    Make the final ACK check under the read lock and queue the release; the
    next write-lock holder applies it in purge_expired_dedup, and the expiry
    sweep drains it on an idle node. A retry that arrives before the release
    waits on ACKs that already arrived and returns at once.
    
    The completion timing now measures a read acquisition, so rename it to
    ack_completion_timing.

